{
 "name": "poly_flip_triple_dirty_parity",
 "face_ring_start": "ignored",
 "face_ring_start_note": "THIS is the fixture the blind spot was found on. Its eight convex quads had diverged from the reference since the day it was written -- we emitted clip tuples, the reference emits strip tuples, the same two triangles with the same winding begun at different corners -- and a rotation-tolerant comparison called that parity. Task 1280 then read the green as evidence that a reference code path 'never ran' and filed a card about a gate that does not exist; a debugger capture refuted it. Measured 2026-08-18 (task 1310): 39 of 61 rings here differed in start only. PART OF THAT IS NOW CLOSED. Task 1320 ported the strip, and the count measured the same way is 23 -- the 16 triangles of the three convex-quad TRIPLE cases (tri_np_one 2, tri_pole_quad3 6, tri_np_twist 8) now match start-and-all, so those three declare \"compared\" below alongside the two that always did. The 23 that remain are all in the mesh.flip cases, which task 1320 did not touch and which stay rotation-tolerant on purpose; their honest record is the divergence they are frozen against, not a start pinned here as if it matched. See doc/tasks/work/1283-fixture-comparison-ignores-tuple-start.md and doc/tasks/work/1320-port-strip.md.",
 "description": "Flipping every face's winding, and triangulating. Neither command had a measured fixture. The flip cells are the only place in this delivery where a direction-sensitive face ring is the ENTIRE assertion -- a flip moves no vertex and changes no count.",
 "source": "frozen reference capture (task 1123, dirty-geometry sweep)",
 "provenance": {
  "schema": 1,
  "source": "live-capture",
  "reference": "ref-editor@11.2v3",
  "method": "command",
  "captured_utc": "2026-08-18",
  "harness": "tools/local/capture (task 1123, dirty-geometry sweep)",
  "task": "1160",
  "notes": "Triangulation is frozen only where the two engines picked the same diagonal: on a reflex or non-planar ring they largely do not (50 of 64 cells diverged), and those are in the divergence lane. What is here is the quad-pole subset where the choice is forced. CHANNELS: the sweep's comparison was never vertex-only -- it compared the vertex multiset, the edge multiset, faces BOTH as ordered rings (winding shows) and as unordered position sets, the material partition, the per-face 'did this face's own tag change', and the post-command selection. Re-checked independently over all 215 frozen cases: ZERO agree on vertices while differing on ordered face rings, so nothing frozen here is a vertex-channel-only agreement. PRECISION: the sweep compared at 1e-4 and this fixture's tolerance matches it. The actual reproduction is far tighter -- 208 of the 215 cases are bit-identical at the dumps' 6 decimals and the remaining 7 agree to 3e-6 or better, that being the worst deviation anywhere in the set. The tolerance is the MEASUREMENT's bound, not the data's."
 },
